// Copy this file to Secrets.staging.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in the
// STAGING Supabase project's values (a SEPARATE project from prod —
// Settings -> API). Keeping dev/staging credentials separate from prod is
// deliberate (Engineering Principles: separate creds per environment), so a
// development run can never read or mutate production data or burn prod quota.
//
// ACTIVATION (once the staging Supabase project actually exists):
//   Point the Debug build config at this file in project.yml, so dev/simulator
//   builds hit staging while Release (TestFlight/App Store) keeps hitting prod:
//
//     configFiles:
//       Debug:   Config/Secrets.staging.xcconfig   # dev / simulator -> staging
//       Release: Config/Secrets.xcconfig           # TestFlight / App Store -> prod
//
//   Then run `xcodegen generate`. Until the real staging file exists, leave
//   BOTH configs on Config/Secrets.xcconfig (the current default) so builds
//   don't break with a missing-file error.
//
// The Gemini key and service_role key are NOT here — they live only as Supabase
// Edge Function secrets, and the staging project needs its own set
// (`supabase secrets set --project-ref <staging-ref> ...`).
//
// xcconfig treats `//` as a comment start, so URLs must break up the double
// slash with an empty macro expansion: https:/$()/example.com

SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR_STAGING_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = YOUR_STAGING_PUBLISHABLE_OR_ANON_KEY
